## Motivation
Implements an OCR3 interface that supports the latest OCR needs:

1. Multi-plugin support: Ability to configure & use multiple OCR plugins
under one contract interface
2. OCR3 plugin compatibility: interface changes (pulled from
liquiditymanager OCR3Abstract)
3. Simplified config digest handling: no longer re-compute config digest
/ no passing of on-chain config, since the source of truth data will
live in the Capability Registry

## Solution
**Focus**: the foucs of the PR is on the **interface** and structure
rather on the exact logic

* Implements a `MultiOCR3Base` abstract contract to match multi-plugin,
Capability Registry and OCR3 plugin interface expectations
* Converts `_transmit` to be internal - implementations are expected to
implement separate `transmit` functions per-DON, since each report logic
will be different, e.g. for CCIP:

```solidity
function transmitExecution(
  // same params as _transmit, except the donId
) {
  // ... handle reporting logic
  _transmit(
    s_transmitDonId,
    // (pass in remaining params from function args)
  );
}

function transmitCommit(
  // same params as _transmit, except the donId
) {
  // ... handle reporting logic
  _transmit(
     s_commitDonId,
     // (pass in remaining params from function args)
  );
}
```

* Sample implementation of `MultiOCR3Base`, with signature skipping
support & multi-DON configs

* Out of scope
  * Config validations & oracle updating logic
  * Transmit msg length handling for different transmit function cases
  * Gas / contract size optimizations

