### Release notes

Small improvement for feeGrowthInside gas. When tickCurrent is fully
outside the range, feeGrowthGlobal cancels out, i.e.
```js
if (tickCurrent < tickLower) {
    feeGrowthInside0 = global0 - (global0 - lower.feeGrowthOutside0)
    - upper.feeGrowthOutside0
    // can be reduced to
    feeGrowthInside0 = lower.feeGrowthOutside0 - upper.feeGrowthOutside0
}
```

If you don't do this, in the tests you have to do:

    vm.expectRevert(bytes4(keccak256("UnsupportedQueryType()")));

Whereas with this change, you can simply import the contract and do:

    vm.expectRevert(UnsupportedQueryType.selector);
